<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela barge hits oil well causing small spill.</title>
<headline>Venezuela barge hits oil well causing small spill.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialized teams worked Friday to contain a small spill in Venezuela's Lake Maracaibo after a barge hit an oil well, authorities said.</p>
<p>&quot;Up to this morning the contingency teams had collected 180 barrels of light crude,&quot; Lenin Herrera head of the Lake Maracaibo Conservation Institute, ICLAM, told Reuters in a brief telephone interview.</p>
<p>The crude collected represented about 80 percent of the total spill, he added.</p>
<p>The spill occurred Thursday when a barge hit a well near the Tia Juana field operated by state oil company Maraven in the southeastern end of the lake.</p>
<p>((-- Omar Lugo, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
